Relay local database design system.

# Purpose

The purpose of this document to define local database schemas and relationships to support offline first architecture.

---

# High Level Architecture

                 Local DB
                    │
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       │            │            │
      users   conversations   messages
                    │
                    │
                    ▼
                Server sync

---

# Schemas

---

## users

users {
id (unique primary key)
username
display_name
avatar_url
updated_at
}

---

## conversations

conversations {
id (unique local primary key)
server_id (server generated UUID, nullable)
type
last_message_id
last_message_preview
last_message_at
updated_at
}

## Constraints

- `id` is unique local generated UUID.
- `server_id` is nullable until server syncronization.

---

## conversation participants

conversation_participants {
conversation_id (unique primary key)
user_id (unique user key)
unread_count
last_read_message_id
joined_at
}

### Relationships

`conversation_participants.conversation_id → conversations.id`
`conversation_participants.user_id → users.id`

### Constraints

A user can not appear twice in a conversation.

---

## messages

messages {
id (server generated UUID, nullable)
client_id (client generated UUID, unique)
conversation_id (conversation reference)
sender_id (user reference)
content
content_type
status
client_created_at
server_created_at (nullable)
attempt_count (retry attempt count)
last_attempt_at (last retry attempt)
last_error (last retry error)
}

## Constraints

- `client_id` is unique.
- `conversation_id` references to `conversations.id`.
- `sender_id` references to `users.id`.
- `id` is the server-generated message ID and is nullable until server acknowledgment.
- `attempt_count` should represent the current retry cycle, not the lifetime of the message.

## Local Status

PENDING
SENDING
SENT
FAILED

## Last error codes

NETWORK_UNAVAILABLE
SOCKET_DISCONNECTED
SEND_TIMEOUT
SERVER_UNAVAILABLE
UNAUTHORIZED

